_n\\leq a_{n+1}$ for all $n \\geq 1$","$a_n = a_{n+1}$ for all $n \\geq 1$","$a_{n+1} \\gt a_n$ for all $n \\geq 1$","$a_n \\gt a_{n+1}$ for all $n \\geq 1$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"969833517ec2ca49a82ed963","time_limit":25},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_monotone_sequence_1702ee35_003","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Which example is decreasing and convergent?","options":["$a_n = n$","$a_n = n+1$","$a_n = \\dfrac{1}{n}$","$a_n = 2n$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"5d7186cd9010639d19a8c539","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_monotone_sequence_1702ee35_004","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Which example is increasing and divergent?","options":["$a_n = \\dfrac{1}{n}$","$a_n = 1$","$a_n = \\dfrac{1}{n+1}$","$a_n = n$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"d378fd78f978e7a3fb0662e3","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_monotone_sequence_1702ee35_005","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which statement about monotone sequences is stated?","options":["They must always converge","They must always diverge","They cannot be bounded","They may converge or diverge"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"8e897f0d335fac9da57d3690","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_monotone_sequence_1702ee35_006","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What extra property ensures convergence for a monotone sequence?","options":["Being strictly increasing","Having positive terms only","Boundedness","Starting at $a_1 = 0$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"2320506d0a5febd2c9c45854","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_monotone_sequence_1702ee35_007","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"How should the constant sequence $a_n=5$ be classified?","options":["It is strictly increasing because the index $n$ keeps increasing.","It is strictly decreasi