iverge","It has no limit concept"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b0d752695a068f4e7e49a4fd","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_monotone_sequence_1702ee35_012","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"Which sequence is monotone but not strictly monotone?","options":["$a_n = 1$ for all $n$","$a_n = n$","$a_n = \\dfrac{1}{n}$","$a_n = -n$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"cddc5da31086aefc4a65be26","time_limit":40},{"id":"expansion_pack_049_monotone_sequence_add_001","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What can be concluded about a decreasing real sequence that is bounded below?","options":["converge","diverge to $-\\infty$","be constant","oscillate"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"163775441b12cc779e59671e","time_limit":30},{"id":"expansion_pack_049_monotone_sequence_add_002","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which condition defines a monotone real sequence?","options":["non-decreasing or non-increasing","both increasing and decreasing","bounded","convergent"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"fa4cff2a187f3e168e4d6629","time_limit":20},{"id":"expansion_pack_049_monotone_sequence_add_003","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What does it mean that a monotone sequence evolves in a single direction?","options":["Its terms must alternate signs.","Its terms must all equal zero.","Its terms move weakly upward or weakly downward.","Its terms must change by the same amount at every step."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a922fc2f45e6c25a25885af3","time_limit":25},{"id":"expansion_pack_049_monotone_sequence_add_004","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Why does a strictly increasing sequence never repeat a value?","options":["Strict increase separates all terms","Boundedness prevents repeated values","Convergence prevents repeated values","Finiteness prevents repeated values"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"13418acf532163b32fec77c1","time_limit":30},{"id":"expansion_pack_049_monotone_sequence_add_005","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Which sequence is decreasing?","options":["$a_n=1/n$","$a_n=n$","$a_n=n+1$","$a_n=2n$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"730c5510dcba6f4fce21578a","time_limit":20},{"id":"expansion_pack_049_monotone_sequence_add_006","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Is the bounded sequence $a_n=(-1)^n$ monotone?","options":["No; its terms alternate","Yes; it is increasing","Yes; it is decreasing","Yes; it is constant"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"50f25b9e76645310cddc2664","time_limit":30},{"id":"expansion_pack_049_monotone_sequence_add_007","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Why does monotonicity alone not guarantee convergence?","options":["Every monotone sequence is finite.","A monotone sequence can be unbounded and divergent.","Every monotone sequence alternates.","A monotone sequence has no order relation."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"e1a7b8088b69cbce935cfa90","time_limit":30},{"id":"expansion_pack_049_monotone_sequence_add_008","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"A sequence is monotone increasing and bounded above. Which result applies?","options":["It is divergent necessarily.","It is convergent.","It is strictly decreasing.","It has no limit if bounded."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"f8be9e4e8c24759089d5bb29","time_limit":30}]}}